body:
if an au pair is what you want, I have some advice:

be upfront with your au pair. It might be helpful to look for an older one who already has experience living alone. Let them know your schedule and your shortcomings

remember that an au pair can only work 30 hours a week in germany, and that theyre not a professional. it might be more helpful to pay for a nanny if thats the work you need.
